# Everything under config/ is runtime state living on the server - application
# databases, Jellyfin metadata, TLS private keys, session stores. None of it is
# reproducible from this repository, so it is ignored wholesale and specific
# paths are re-included by exception.
#
# Adding a config file that should be tracked means adding a matching ! rule,
# and each level has to be un-ignored in turn: git will not descend into an
# ignored directory to find an exception inside it.
config/*
!config/sonarr/

config/sonarr/*
!config/sonarr/scripts/

# Reverse proxy configuration used to live here as SWAG nginx confs. It is now
# ingress/Caddyfile, which is a normal tracked file outside config/.

# Ignore the environment file containing sensitive values.
# The wildcard matters as much as the exact name: editing .env tends to leave
# .env.bak, .env.orig or .env.20260811 next to it, and a bare `.env` rule does
# not match any of those. This repository is public, so an unignored copy is a
# credential leak waiting for one `git add -A`.
.env
.env.*
!.env.sample

# Transcode scratch (DOCKER_VOLUME_CACHE), regenerable and large.
cache/
